# explore-sector survey config -- copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in.
#
#   cp .env.example .env   &&   $EDITOR .env
#
# `explore-live.sh` sources `.env` from this folder (set -a), then runs the
# survey against an ALREADY-RUNNING, ALREADY-IN-GAME live client -- it does NOT
# start our docker stack and never launches the client itself. The survey drives
# the client entirely through the injected enbmod Lua command channel (no OCR,
# no screenshots), so the character must already be in space.
#
# Only the values that actually vary per machine live here. Every threshold knob
# the driver reads (VISIT_K, warp/gate timeouts, relocation budget, hang seconds)
# has a baked-in default and is NOT listed -- override one only if you have a
# reason to. Do not paste server IPs or the repo path in here.

# ---- REQUIRED -------------------------------------------------------------

# The character the survey is for. It is also the character a LOCAL-stack relogin
# re-enters (explore-live.sh feeds it to the login skill's ENB_LOGIN_CHAR). In
# manual/live mode a hard hang HALTS instead of relogging, so there it is just
# the label on the run.
ENB_EXPLORE_CHARACTER_NAME=YourCharacter

# Where a whole survey lives: per-sector ledgers (<Sector>.json), actions.log,
# and captures/. Point it OUTSIDE the repo so progress + pcaps are not in git.
# Re-using the same path RESUMES a survey (completed sectors are skipped, and a
# half-done sector picks up from its persisted visited rows).
ENB_EXPLORE_WORKDIR=/absolute/path/to/your/survey-workdir

# ---- LIVE-MODE DEFAULTS (explore-live.sh forces/sets these; override if needed) ----

# 1 = you own the client + proxy; the survey never kills/relaunches them. On a
# hard client hang the survey HALTS and asks you to relaunch + re-run (the ledger
# persists, so the re-run resumes). explore-live.sh forces this on -- listed here
# only for visibility.
ENB_EXPLORE_MANUAL_CLIENT=1

# Capture the real WINE proxy (host process, exact `comm` name) instead of the
# dockerized FreyaProxy. This is what a live client connects through.
ENB_EXPLORE_PROXY_NAME=Net7Proxy.exe

# 1 = start the per-sector packet capture at char-select (the entry handshake),
# then one file per sector. Needs the capture worker installed once:
#   sudo bash scripts/pcap-install.sh
# A LOCAL freya run forces this to 0 (owner rule: never pcap a local run).
ENB_PCAP=1

# ---- OPTIONAL TUNING ------------------------------------------------------

# X display the WINE client renders on (defaults to :0).
# DISPLAY=:0

# Hard cap on sectors driven in one survey run (default 40).
# ENB_MAX_SECTORS=40

# Seconds the enbmod Lua channel may stay silent before the client is declared
# hung (default 150 -- comfortably above a gate-transit load screen).
# ENB_LUA_HANG_SECS=150
